/name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>MURATA, KENICHI</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SAITO, JUNYA</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SONY CORPORATION</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>KATAYAMA YASUSHI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>KITAZATO NAOHISA</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>MURATA KENICHI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>SAITO JUNYA</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KATAYAMA, YASUSHI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KITAZATO, NAOHISA</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>MURATA, KENICHI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SAITO, JUNYA</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A client transmits Event::Subscribe("DSI_CHANGED") to a server. The server returns an event number preset for the "DSI_CHANGED" event.  After obtaining the event number, the client transmits Event::notify to the server and requests a certain notification of occurrence of an event including a "DSI_CHANGED".  When the DSI of the received carousel is changed, namely, a "DSI_CHANGED" event occurs at a certain timing after the reception of the Event::notify, the server transmits the event number corresponding to the "DSI_CHANGED" event to the client in response to the Event::notify.  For the period from the time when the server notifies the client of the occurrence of the event number till the time when the client transmits Session::detach to the server, the contents of the carousel before the event number occurs is used continually.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>Un client transmet un Evénement::Abonnement("DSI_CHANGE") à un serveur. Le serveur renvoie un numéro d'événement préattribué à l'événement "DSI_CHANGE". Après obtention du numéro d'événement, le client transmet un Evénement::Notification au serveur et demande une notification d'occurrence spécifique d'un événement incluant "DSI_CHANGE". Lorsque le DSI du carrousel reçu est changé, c'est-à-dire qu'un événement "DSI_CHANGE" a lieu à un moment donné après la réception de l'Evénement::Notification, le serveur transmet au client le numéro d'événement correspondant à l'événement "DSI_CHANGE", en réponse à l'Evénement::Notification. Pendant la durée au cours de laquelle le serveur notifie le client de l'occurrence du numéro d'événement jusqu'au moment où le client transmet au serveur la Session::Interruption, le contenu du carrousel est utilisé de manière continue, et ce jusqu'à l'occurrence du numéro d'événement.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>